meta {
  name: drawer map
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}inventory/drawer-map/?search=motor
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  search: motor
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  The cabinet as a 2D grid (FR-7.5): `rows`, then `drawers`, then `chambers`.
  Each chamber has a `state`:

  - `EMPTY`: no component assigned (grey)
  - `OCCUPIED`: component present, total above minimum (green)
  - `LOW_STOCK`: component total at or below its minimum (amber)
  - `OUT_OF_STOCK`: component assigned but this chamber holds 0 (red)

  `search` highlights (`highlighted: true`) every chamber whose component
  name or part number matches (FR-7.7). Any role.


  ## API example response
  {
    "cabinet": {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Main Cabinet",
      "rows": 3,
      "columns": 4
    },
    "summary": {
